# Fixtures are byte-exact. The conformance corpus asserts byte offsets into
# input.md (FR-MD-003), so a checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF shifts every
# range in every expected AST and the suite fails on Windows and nowhere else
# — which is exactly how it was found. The same goes for the fuzz seed corpus,
# where the input is the bytes.
#
# This also matters ahead of P0.2: the frontmatter round-trip fixtures are
# asserted byte-for-byte, and preserving line endings is itself a requirement
# there (FR-VLT-015).
testdata/**            text eol=lf
**/testdata/**         text eol=lf

# The frontmatter corpus is the exception, and it has to be. Preserving a file's
# own line endings is the requirement under test there (FR-VLT-017, FR-MD-033),
# and roundtrip/crlf.md exists to prove Sherd does. Normalizing it to LF deletes
# the fixture's reason to exist while leaving it looking fine — which is what
# happened the moment the corpus landed, caught by the test that asserts the
# fixture's own bytes. These files are committed exactly as they are.
testdata/frontmatter/** -text
